# Data

## File

`YRBS_2023_National.rda` contains one R object, `yrbs_2023`: the 2023 national Youth Risk Behavior Survey (YRBS) public-use data, with 20,103 students and 269 variables.

MD5 checksum of the file used for the paper: `692307f4674bc97292ab69c380b136be`

`yrbs_analysis.R` checks this checksum each time it runs and warns if the file differs.

## Source

Centers for Disease Control and Prevention, 2023 National YRBS, ASCII data file: https://www.cdc.gov/yrbs/data/index.html

Variable definitions follow the CDC's *2023 YRBS Data User's Guide*: https://www.cdc.gov/yrbs/media/pdf/2023/2023_National_YRBS_Data_Users_Guide508.pdf

Date downloaded: 8/12/2026

ASCII file was converted to .rda by Aida Pacheco-Applegate via personal communication for a differnt project. 

## Variables used in the analysis

| Variable | Meaning | Coding |
|---|---|---|
| `sex` | "What is your sex?" (does not specify sex assigned at birth) | 1 = female, 2 = male |
| `q65` | "Are you transgender?" | 1 = no, 2 = yes, 3 = not sure, 4 = does not know what the question is asking |
| `qn14` | Did not go to school on at least 1 day in the past 30 days because they felt unsafe | 1 = yes, 2 = no |
| `qn24` | Bullied on school property in the past 12 months | 1 = yes, 2 = no |
| `qn25` | Electronically bullied in the past 12 months | 1 = yes, 2 = no |
| `qnclose2people` | Agree or strongly agree that they feel close to people at school | 1 = yes, 2 = no (not sure, disagree, or strongly disagree) |
| `weight`, `stratum`, `psu` | Survey design: sampling weight, stratum, primary sampling unit | |

Note: `stweight` in this file is students' body weight in kilograms, not a sampling weight.
